{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Peter and Online Dating"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Your Online Profile"}, {"type": "position", "content": 8}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 11}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Use expressions about relationships and feelings in a range of social and work contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Writes an exchange of written communications about asking for and giving advice on problems with technology or gadgets through the correct use of spelling, grammar, vocabulary, level of formality, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriated to this level"}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Writes an exchange of written communications about asking for and giving advice on problems with technology or gadgets through the correct use of spelling, grammar, vocabulary, level of formality, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriated to this level"}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Writes an exchange of written communications about asking for and giving advice on problems with technology or gadgets through the correct use of spelling, grammar, vocabulary, level of formality, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriated to this level"}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Writes an exchange of written communications about asking for and giving advice on problems with technology or gadgets through the correct use of spelling, grammar, vocabulary, level of formality, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriated to this level"}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Writes an exchange of written communications about asking for and giving advice on problems with technology or gadgets through the correct use of spelling, grammar, vocabulary, level of formality, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriated to this level"}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Writes an exchange of written communications about asking for and giving advice on problems with technology or gadgets through the correct use of spelling, grammar, vocabulary, level of formality, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriated to this level"}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Writes an exchange of written communications about asking for and giving advice on problems with technology or gadgets through the correct use of spelling, grammar, vocabulary, level of formality, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriated to this level"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn7le11ob08re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Present Perfect Continuous vs Present Perfect + <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">Since</span></span> and <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">For</span></span> for Duration"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use both of these tenses for finished and unfinished actions.<br/><br/>The Present Perfect tense can be used to talk about unfinished actions that started in the past and are still true in the present. You often include the words <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">since </span> and <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">for</span> to talk about the unfinished action."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You often use the Present Perfect tense when we're talking about how much or how many. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example: <br/>  <span class=\"italic\">I've not e-mailed my friend <span class=\"strong\">for</span> a long time.<br/> Steve has drunk two cups of coffee already!</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can also use the Present Perfect continuous can also be used to talk about unfinished actions that started in the past and are still true in the present. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use the Present Perfect Continuous tense to emphasize the length of time that has passed. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "  Example: <br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">She's been working on her online profile <span class=\"strong\">for</span> a long time.<br/> Julie has been drinking the same coffee <span class=\"strong\">since</span> early this morning!</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": " I have been fascinated by different ideas, religions and cultures <span class=\"strong\">since</span> I was a child."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I have been single <span class=\"strong\">for</span> a few years now."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I have been working <span class=\"strong\">since</span> my late teens."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Phrasal Verbs "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Phrasal verbs consist of a verb and one or more prepositions. They are often used, especially in informal spoken English. The meaning of phrasal verbs is often completely different from the meaning of the verb alone."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Phrasal verbs can either be separable or inseparable."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Separable phrasal verbs consist of two parts. They always require an object."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The object of a phrasal verb can go either between the verb and the preposition or after the preposition."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"underline\">Examples</span>:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">looked up</span> the word in the dictionary. </span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">looked</span> the word <span class=\"strong\">up</span> in the dictionary.</span><br/>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "  If the object of the sentence is a pronoun, it must go between the two parts of the phrasal verb. <br>  <span class=\"underline\">Example</span>: <br/><span class=\"italic\">I looked <span class=\"strong\">it</span> up in the dictionary.</span>  "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Some phrasal verbs are inseparable, so the verb must be directly followed by its preposition or adverb. Otherwise, the meaning of the phrasal verb will be incorrect. <br/>Some inseparable phrasal verbs never use an object."}, {"type": "text", "content": " <span class=\"underline\">Examples</span>:<br/> <ul><li>settle down= get married   <br/> <span class=\"italic\"> I would like to settle down with the right person.</span></li> <li>eat out = eat at a restaurant    <br/>    <span class=\"italic\">I love going to see live music  eating out at interesting restaurants.</span></li><li> break up = end a relationship  <br/> <span class=\"italic\"> I would rather stay as a singleton rather than be part of an unhappy couple, only to break up later.</span></li></ul>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "gregarious"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "enjoying the company of other people"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She has a gregarious nature."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le11ob08aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you hear in a conversation about relationships and technology."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "around the corner "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "in the near future"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There is someone for you just around the corner."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le11ob08aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to commit"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to decide to give your love, support, or effort to someone or something in a serious or permanent way"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I am not afraid to commit to someone."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le11ob08aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to fall into place "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "for things to work out well"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Things just seem to be falling into place for James and I."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le11ob08aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to settle down"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to begin to live a quiet and steady life by getting a regular job, getting married"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I am ready to settle down."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le11ob08aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "singleton"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person or thing occurring singly, especially an individual set apart from others."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:I would rather stay as a happy singleton rather than end up part of an unhappy couple, only to break up later."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le11ob08aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "aspirations"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something that a person wants very much to achieve"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:i have a lot of goals and aspirations."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le11ob08aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to get in touch"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to get in contact with someone"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Why not 